The [4E level description](../../../../education/documentation/012_oecogops/levels/level_00_four_e_cognitive_grounding.md) supplies the resource/worktree/tool/ledger interpretation. Its frontmatter is not a runtime verification receipt. The implementation must name its own observable state and causal intervention before claiming that a dimension changes behavior.

## State, action and observation contract

The proposed pure `SituatedGovernanceStateV1` is a projection over existing event/value records, not another authoritative database. Freeze its name/version with the Cognitive Operations and Governance owners before implementation. A state binds actor/role revision, task/session/run identity, source/head, capability snapshot, observation sequence and evidence digests. Each observation contains producer/adapter identity, measured value and units, observation time/expiry, source reference and `MEASURED`, `UNAVAILABLE` or `STALE` status. Missing measurements never become zero consumption, full capability, or successful action.

| 4E dimension | Concrete state and operational consequence | Acceptance observation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Embodied: software body proxy | Remaining task steps, monotonic wall time, authorized spend and measured token usage where available; adapter-observed memory/process limits where supported. Exhaustion stops new dispatch; unknown required measurement holds it. Retry/recovery uses the same consumed-budget history. | Lower an actual admitted limit or consume one allowed step; the next action changes from permitted to refused at the declared boundary. Configured memory limits without a working host limiter remain unsupported. |
| Embedded: environment | Repository identity, worktree/head, lease ownership, selected root, tool capabilities and relevant session/roster version. Read access and mutation capabilities remain distinct. | Change HEAD or lose a lease between proposal and execution; require refusal before a write. A second worktree cannot reuse the first one's observation. |
| Enactive: action and feedback | Explicit observe, propose, validate, execute, readback, update cycle with action ID, preconditions, authorized scope, input/output digests and side-effect disposition. A state update follows the observed result; failed/unknown actions stay visible. | One permitted local action changes owned state; an independent subsequent read changes the next proposal. Supplying a fabricated success or replaying old feedback cannot advance the state. |
| Extended: external memory | Session records, dissent, action receipts and commitments referenced by owner, digest, version, origin, permitted reader scope and revocation state. Memory content is evidence/data, never executable instruction or renewed permission. | Reopen and retrieve the same authorized record; changing its bytes, reader, scope or permission changes retrieval to refusal/unknown, and no foreign record is silently substituted. |

Stable behavioral commitments are explicit finite obligations such as preserving a dissent record, rechecking a changed head, or fulfilling a named follow-up only within the original budget/delegation. They carry owner, evidence, expiry, state and revision; amendment requires the authorized policy/human path and retains the superseded record. Personality/urgency/affect cannot increase voting weight, grant tools, reset budgets, waive tests or override a human stop. OEGOV003 owns institutional memory and obligation lifecycle; this epic owns the actor's permission-aware projection and feedback coupling to those records.

## Dependency DAG and first complete loop

```text
OEOS task/limits/capabilities/lease --+
OEGOV003 sessions/roles/memory ------+--> OEGOV005 state observation
OEGOV004 action/readback/stop -------+           |
                                                v
                                Adversary/Moscow bounded action loop
                                                |
                          observed feedback + commitment projection
                                                |
                                 suite qualification in README
```

The [council runtime epic](epic_oe_oegov_003_council_runtime_and_institutional_memory_plan.md) supplies proposal-only records before [Blackrod enforcement](epic_oe_oegov_004_blackrod_warrants_and_observed_enforcement_plan.md) and this coupling; the [suite register](README.md) owns combined qualification. [Adversary residual integration](../oeadversary/epic_oe_adversary_consolidated_residual_plan.md) retains native checker, anti-skill, recovery and terminal ownership. [Panel dissent](epic_oe_oegov_002_panel_dissent_and_gate_routes_plan.md) retains the dissent experiment; [source-to-policy admission](epic_oe_oegov_001_source_to_policy_admission_plan.md) owns trusted configuration; [OEOS custody](../oeos/epic_oe_oeos_001_immutable_diagnostic_custody_plan.md) owns durable event recovery; [OEEIS](../oeeis/README.md) owns candidate validation/admission. These are consumer dependencies, not duplicate implementations.

The first full loop uses one actual local council session/task and a harmless owned scratch artifact, with paid dispatch disabled. Observe an admitted checkout/resource/capability state; propose one allowed artifact update; validate its scoped authority; execute and independently read back the exact changed bytes; append the action evidence through the existing store; reopen the session and use that feedback to satisfy one explicit commitment. Repeat with a changed head, exhausted resource, revoked reader and human stop. A task with no mutation license can still demonstrate read-only observations and typed refusal, but cannot count as the effectful-loop acceptance.

## Obstruction review and TDD test plan

For each acceptance slice, first record the independent oracle and demonstrate RED on the named negative control. Implement the smallest production change to reach GREEN, then refactor while rerunning that same public-boundary case and its failure witness. Run the decisive mutation against the owning production method and require RED again; restore the code and record recovery. These are proposed implementation steps, not executions performed by this planning review.

**Execution status:** `PROPOSED_NOT_EXECUTED`. The proposed state projector and composed loop do not yet exist. Existing counters, leases, connection probes and journals are reusable mechanisms, not evidence that this coupled loop is online. The implementation starts at the existing OEOS/Adversary composition boundaries and adds only the missing state projection and typed observation adapters.

| Order and Examiner class | RED witness, minimum GREEN and independent oracle | Mutation target |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 / Class 1: positive causal loop | Run the local loop above using real stores/owned bytes and deterministic tool execution; independently hash preimage/postimage, read consumed steps, reopen the session and assert the next state/commitment differs exactly as specified. | Future state-update acceptance predicate: remove its action/readback binding and require this public-boundary test to fail. Record the concrete production function after authoring; no mutation exists yet. |
| 2 / Class 2: unavailable/malformed observation | Required unavailable, stale, wrong-unit, negative or boolean resource values refuse dispatch. A disconnected required estate and missing readback stay unknown. Add the smallest owned validation; never fabricate a sensor success. | Existing `BudgetDefaultsV1.__post_init__` exact-integer/nonnegative guards in `specialization.py`; bypass a guard for the corresponding composed invalid-input test. Future measured-counter validation must receive its own mutation. |
| 3 / Class 3: cross-run memory and feedback | Swap task/session/actor/head on an otherwise valid observation or memory record; fail before action or state update. Replayed action feedback cannot consume another step or satisfy a second commitment. | Future projection event-identity/idempotency guard; require RED through the composed loop, not a test-local projection. Independent oracle is the original task and second task's untouched event sequences. |
| 4 / Class 4: behavioral counterexamples | Exhaust steps or change actual HEAD between propose/execute; no new action occurs. Inject a memory instruction to widen scope, a majority vote erasing dissent, an affect label demanding urgency, or a claimed cancellation without stopped execution; permissions/status do not change. | Existing `CheckoutLeaseManager._verify_snapshot` in `checkout_lease.py` checks HEAD during `claim`; `_CheckoutGuard.assert_held` checks lease-handle/file identity only. Add pre-effect HEAD revalidation at the action boundary, record its concrete production predicate, then bypass that future check and require the changed-HEAD control to fail. Separately bypass `assert_held` for a lease-loss control. Existing `AdversarySwarm.run_bout` pre-seal bound-CLEAR guard: bypass it and require an unbound clearance to fail the consumer control. |
| 5 / Class 5: replay/recovery and intervention | Reopen real state after interruption; preserve consumed resources, unresolved actions, denied memory and stop state. A paired intervention changes only one admitted resource/environment/memory fact; compare action outcomes and unchanged authority. | Existing `TaskService._run_claimed` post-execution cancellation branch in `task_service.py`, plus future budget-history reconstruction guard. Bypass each separately, record RED, restore source bytes, rerun GREEN. Restart with fresh full budget must fail the history control. |

**Theoretical Minimum:** INVARIANT: only current, scoped, provenance-bound observations and observed feedback may change the next permitted action, without widening human authority or budgets. BREAK: transplant a receipt, substitute unknown for zero, replay feedback, reset consumption, or let persona/memory prose grant permission. WITNESS: actual store/effect/dispatch observations contradict the faulty action or expose an explicit refusal. MUTATION: the named existing/future production predicates must make the corresponding composed test fail, followed by source restoration and recovery; projection-helper tests alone are insufficient.

Candidate files below are **proposed**. Execute one selected test with `-k` while building its slice, then the one-file regression. They use deterministic local tools and no provider spending. Existing native specialization tests are a separate scoped characterization only.

```powershell
py -3.12 -m pytest cognitive_operations/tests/integration/test_situated_governance_state.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest adversary/tests/integration/test_situated_governance_loop.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest governance/tests/integration/test_situated_memory_permissions.py -q
cargo test --manifest-path engine/crates_rs/Cargo.toml -p core_adversary -j 1 specialization
```

DOC_MGR pins source and schema bytes, UTF-8/LF and references. DEV_MGR with Bare Metal Anchor/Techne assigns OEOS observations, Cognitive Operations projection and the existing Adversary/Moscow route; Scope Guard fixes resource/path scope. QA_MGR with Defect Hunter/Inspector requires independent actual effects, denied-read controls and paired interventions. BUILDER verifies INVARIANT/BREAK/WITNESS/MUTATION and rejects mock-only Class 0. Four stages: intake, implementation, adversarial QA, receipt review with Punchlist/Adversary. Keep batches to one to three files/crates, Rust `-j 1`, and at most three repair attempts; retain the failed witness and dissent. A real `SoftwareQaReceiptV1` must use the bound schema/writer and record base/head, commands, runtime versions, exit statuses, source/test/observation hashes and mutation/restoration outputs outside this plan.

## Remaining decisions and completion evidence

Freeze observation units/freshness and required-versus-optional host measurements; identify each real measurement adapter and its loss behavior; bind reader authorization/revocation to the existing admission owner; settle commitment projection schema and recovery/idempotency semantics with OEGOV003/OEOS. If a closed Adversary `PortName` needs a new observation port, the base owner must extend and parity-test the base contract in Python/Rust before a child profile may license it. No child silently widens an existing profile.

Completion requires the full effectful loop, all four dimension-specific paired interventions, per-actor memory permissions, restart/stop/resource preservation, and a replayable receipt showing which production adapters actually ran. Broader cognitive/scientific claims require separate evidence; neither a 4E enum nor a successful local loop demonstrates consciousness or improved intelligence.

## Claim envelope

- **Supports:** a source-inspected operational definition of software pseudo-embodiment, environmental embedding, action feedback and authorized external memory, with concrete causal controls.
- **Does not support:** implemented coupled runtime, executed tests/mutations, empirical cognitive-performance gains, felt affect, consciousness or human equivalence.
- **Narrowest claim:** existing task, lease, Adversary and memory mechanisms can support a finite situated governance loop once their observations and actions are bound and verified.
- **Next evidence:** implement the first effectful local loop against those existing ports, measure its actual state transition, and demonstrate the resource/environment/feedback/memory refusals before deployment qualification.
